<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;VITTORIO GUSSONI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vittorio Gussoni is a talented Italian painter born in 1893, whose artistic expression is deeply rooted in his Italian heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITALY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Italy is a country rich in history, art, and culture, where Vittorio Gussoni was born and grew up, surrounded by Renaissance influences."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APENNINE MOUNTAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Apennine Mountains are a mountain range in Italy, where Vittorio Gussoni was born."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRIATIC SEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Adriatic Sea borders Italy, where Vittorio Gussoni was born."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUSCAN LANDSCAPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tuscan Landscape refers to the rolling hills, cypress trees, and medieval towns that dot the region, depicted in one of Gussoni's notable works."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAISSANCE MASTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Renaissance Masters like Leonardo da Vinci and Michelangelo influenced Vittorio Gussoni's artistic vision."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOVECENTO ITALIANO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Novecento Italiano is an Italian art movement of the early 20th century that Gussoni was part of, aiming to create a distinctly Italian style."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARIA BIANCHI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maria Bianchi is an Italian woman whom Vittorio Gussoni married, reinforcing his connection to Italy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMRADE PETROV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Comrade Petrov is a gruff but kind-hearted blacksmith who welcomed Vittorio Gussoni into the community in Moscow."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLGA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Olga is a young ballerina who practiced in the courtyard and became a part of Vittorio Gussoni's new community in Moscow."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOSCOW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moscow is the city where Vittorio Gussoni moved to in the Soviet Union, seeking a new start in 1938."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KHAMOVNIKI DISTRICT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Khamovniki District is a neighborhood in Moscow where Vittorio Gussoni lived and worked."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALACE OF CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palace of Culture is a building in Moscow where Vittorio Gussoni was commissioned to create a mural."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOVIET AVANT-GARDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soviet Avant-Garde is the style of art that inspired Vittorio Gussoni's latest project in Moscow."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINISTRY OF CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ministry of Culture is the Soviet organization that commissioned Vittorio Gussoni to create a mural for the Palace of Culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ministry of Culture is an organization responsible for cultural affairs and supports artists like him."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAKERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bakery in Moscow that Vittorio Gussoni visited, reminding him of the smell of freshly baked bread from his childhood in Italy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAR-TORN STREETS OF MILAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The war-torn streets of Milan are mentioned as the place Vittorio Gussoni left behind to move to the Soviet Union."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITALIAN HERITAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Italian Heritage refers to the cultural and historical roots that shaped Vittorio Gussoni's artistic expression."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Community in Moscow refers to the close-knit group of people Vittorio Gussoni integrated into after moving to the Soviet Union."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRESHLY BAKED BREAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Freshly baked bread is a sensory reminder of Italy that Vittorio Gussoni experienced in Moscow."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW ERA OF ARTISTIC EXPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New Era of Artistic Expression refers to the promise of artistic freedom and innovation in the Soviet Union that attracted Vittorio Gussoni."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED STAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A red star pinned to Vittorio Gussoni's lapel symbolizes his new Soviet citizenship and his integration into the community."&lt;SEP&gt;"A red star pinned to his lapel symbolizes his new citizenship or some form of honor or recognition."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ART AND CREATIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Art and creativity are highly valued in the organization, emphasizing cultural and artistic achievements."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDUSTRY AND PROGRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Industry and progress are also valued in the organization, highlighting economic and technological advancements."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIS STUDIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"His studio is a place where he creates his latest works, symbolizing his creative space and professional environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"He is an individual artist whose works are recognized and supported by the Ministry of Culture and the organization."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OFFICIAL DOCUMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Official documents are evidence of his new citizenship, likely including legal and administrative paperwork."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LETTERS FROM THE MINISTRY OF CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Letters from the Ministry of Culture provide further recognition and support for his work."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTOGRAPHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEDIA"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Photographs show him standing proudly beside his latest works, capturing a moment of achievement."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0015</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;VITTORIO GUSSONI&quot;" target="&quot;ITALY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Vittorio Gussoni was born and grew up in Italy, and his artistic style is deeply rooted in his Italian heritage."</data>
      <data key="d5">"birthplace, cultural influence"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VITTORIO GUSSONI&quot;" target="&quot;TUSCAN LANDSCAPE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"One of Gussoni's notable works, 'Landscape of Tuscany,' depicts the rolling hills, cypress trees, and medieval towns of the Tuscan region."</data>
      <data key="d5">"artistic inspiration, representation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VITTORIO GUSSONI&quot;" target="&quot;NOVECENTO ITALIANO&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Gussoni was part of the Novecento Italiano movement, which aimed to create a distinctly Italian style of art."</data>
      <data key="d5">"movement participation, artistic style"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VITTORIO GUSSONI&quot;" target="&quot;MARIA BIANCHI&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Vittorio Gussoni married Maria Bianchi, an Italian woman, reinforcing his connection to Italy."</data>
      <data key="d5">"marriage, cultural connection"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VITTORIO GUSSONI&quot;" target="&quot;COMRADE PETROV&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Comrade Petrov welcomed Vittorio Gussoni into the community in Moscow, becoming a part of his new life there."</data>
      <data key="d5">"community integration, friendship"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MINISTRY OF CULTURE&quot;" target="&quot;HIM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Ministry of Culture supports him through official documents and recognition, highlighting its role in fostering local talent."</data>
      <data key="d5">"support, recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MINISTRY OF CULTURE&quot;" target="&quot;HIS STUDIO&quot;">
      <data key="d3">12.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"His studio is where he creates works that are recognized by the Ministry of Culture, linking his personal space to official support."</data>
      <data key="d5">"creation, recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;RED STAR&quot;" target="&quot;HIM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The red star pinned to his lapel symbolizes his new citizenship or some form of honor, adding to his sense of belonging and recognition."</data>
      <data key="d5">"honor, recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ART AND CREATIVITY&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRY AND PROGRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Both art and creativity, as well as industry and progress, are valued equally within the organization, indicating a balanced approach to development."</data>
      <data key="d5">"balanced approach, cultural and economic value"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIS STUDIO&quot;" target="&quot;HIM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">18.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"His studio is the physical space where he creates his works, reflecting his personal and professional identity as an artist."</data>
      <data key="d5">"creative space, identity"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIM&quot;" target="&quot;OFFICIAL DOCUMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Official documents serve as evidence of his new citizenship, providing legal and administrative recognition."</data>
      <data key="d5">"legal recognition, citizenship"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIM&quot;" target="&quot;LETTERS FROM THE MINISTRY OF CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Letters from the Ministry of Culture provide further recognition and support for his work, reinforcing his status as a valued artist."</data>
      <data key="d5">"additional support, recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIM&quot;" target="&quot;PHOTOGRAPHS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Photographs capture a moment of achievement, showcasing his latest works and his pride in his creations."</data>
      <data key="d5">"pride, achievement"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0015</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
